        "kernelId": "econ/natural-experiment",
        "term": "Natural experiment",
        "claims": [
          "A natural experiment uses a policy change or external event affecting one group but not another to estimate a causal effect from observational data.",
          "The causal claim is credible only if the two groups were comparable apart from the change.",
          "The effect can be attributed to the policy rather than to a confounding factor only when that comparability holds."
        ],
        "attribution": [
          "OpenStax Principles of Macroeconomics 2e, Ch. 2"
